{"availability":"available","full":"WASTEFI-AFRICA/wastefi-frontend","name":"wastefi-frontend","description":"Mobile-first web app for WasteFi collectors, collection points and administrators, with a public live stats page. Next.js and TypeScript.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":6,"forks":4,"created":"2026-09-14T19:35:01Z","updated":"2026-10-09T17:38:32Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://wastefi-frontend.vercel.app","topics":["financial-inclusion","nextjs","offline-first","pwa","react","tailwindcss","typescript","waste-management"],"demo":"https://wastefi-frontend.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T14:53:08.354Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T14:53:08.354Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T14:53:08.354Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T14:53:08.354Z","stars":6,"forks":4}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Progressive web app for WasteFi, a platform that pays waste collectors in emerging markets for verified recyclable material drop-offs. Collectors submit collections and track earnings; collection points verify deliveries and manage inventory; administrators review fraud signals and platform activity.","It is built mobile-first and offline-first, because the people using it are often on a low-end Android phone with intermittent connectivity. A collection submitted with no signal is queued locally and synced when the network returns.","Only /stats is connected to the backend. The screens behind sign-in (dashboard, wallet, collections, profile, and the collection-point and admin screens) render hard-coded sample data, and each shows a notice saying so. The sign-in form is a demo: it signs in a placeholder user without calling the API, although the API's own login is real and tested. Connecting those screens is the main piece of remaining work."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/WASTEFI-AFRICA/wastefi-frontend/blob/main/README.md"